# Frontend Services & Routing

## File Roles
*   `views/` — pages registered in `router.js`.
*   `components/` — shared forms, nav, dialogs.
*   `services/services.js` — authenticated axios instance; domain modules in `*Services.js`.
*   `services/publicServices.js` — unauthenticated client for `/public` and public donate.
*   `config/utils.js` — `setStore`, `getStore`, `removeItem`, org helpers (localStorage JSON).
*   `utils/` — pure helpers only; no HTTP calls.

## Domain Service Modules
*   One file per domain: `authServices.js`, `tripServices.js`, `donationServices.js`, etc.
*   Default-export an object of methods; each method calls `apiClient` (or public client) and returns the promise.
*   No axios calls inside views or components — always go through `*Services.js`.

## Axios Client (`services/services.js`)
*   Dev `baseURL`: `http://localhost:3200/trips/`; prod: `/trips/`.
*   `withCredentials: true`.
*   Request interceptor: attach `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from `Utils.getStore("user")`; attach `X-Acting-Organization-Id` from effective org when set.
*   On unauthorized responses: clear `user`, dispatch logout event, `Router.push({ name: "login" })`.
*   FormData uploads: delete `Content-Type` header so the browser sets the boundary.

## Router Conventions (`router.js`)
*   vue-router 4 with `createWebHistory`.
*   Named routes (e.g. `home`, `tripView`, `tripBrowse`, `donorTrip`).
*   `props: true` on routes with params.
*   `router.beforeEach` — auth and role guards per `auth-patterns.mdc` / Feature specs (system admin cannot browse-apply).

## Cross-Component Events
Dispatch `window` `CustomEvent`s (`user-logged-in`, `user-logged-out`, `user-updated`) when auth or org context changes so MenuBar / Home refresh without prop drilling.

## Production Deploy
Copy `public/.htaccess` to `dist/` on build — SPA fallback rewrite and cache headers for hashed assets.
